# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vedic Vaibhav frontend — environment template
#
# Copy to .env. Like backend/.env, this file holds ONE thing: the mode.
#
#   APP_MODE=development  ->  .env.development  (committed, localhost API)
#   APP_MODE=production   ->  .env.production   (committed, live API)
#
# The switch is applied in next.config.ts. Next.js normally picks the mode file
# from the COMMAND (`next dev` vs `next build`) and gives plain `.env` the
# LOWEST precedence — next.config.ts inverts that so this file wins, matching
# the backend.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#   real shell var  >  .env.local (gitignored)  >  .env.<APP_MODE>
#
# Two constraints worth knowing:
#   * NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are baked into the browser bundle at `pnpm build`
#     time. Set the mode BEFORE building. `pnpm build` refuses to run with
#     APP_MODE=development so localhost URLs can't reach production.
#   * APP_MODE is deliberately NOT called NODE_ENV. Next owns NODE_ENV (dev
#     server vs optimized build); overriding it yields a broken prod bundle.
#
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are exposed to the browser — never put a secret
# in any of these files.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

APP_MODE=development
